<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Flow xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <apiVersion>59.0</apiVersion>
    <areMetricsLoggedToDataCloud>false</areMetricsLoggedToDataCloud>
    <decisions>
        <name>Cadence_Target_Filter</name>
        <label>Cadence Target Filter</label>
        <locationX>644</locationX>
        <locationY>252</locationY>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>Default Outcome</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>leads</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>$Record.TargetId</leftValueReference>
                <operator>StartsWith</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <stringValue>00Q</stringValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Get_Lead</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>leads</label>
        </rules>
        <rules>
            <name>contacts</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>$Record.TargetId</leftValueReference>
                <operator>StartsWith</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <stringValue>003</stringValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Get_Contact</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>contacts</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <decisions>
        <name>Does_Contact_Exist</name>
        <label>Does Contact Exist?</label>
        <locationX>710</locationX>
        <locationY>468</locationY>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>Contact Not Found</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Contact_Exists</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>Get_Contact</leftValueReference>
                <operator>IsNull</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>false</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Remove_contacts_from_cases</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Contact Exists</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <decisions>
        <description>Check if the Lead was found</description>
        <name>Does_Lead_Exist</name>
        <label>Does Lead Exist?</label>
        <locationX>182</locationX>
        <locationY>468</locationY>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>Lead Not Found</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Lead_Exists</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>Get_Lead</leftValueReference>
                <operator>IsNull</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>false</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Delete_leads</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Lead Exists</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <description>Added Start Critiria that the Target Id must not be null (so we aren&apos;t reprocessing cadence trackers where we have already deleted the target)
Removed the step that updated the Lead/Contact Age fields before they were deleted (this seems to have been related to a batch process in RingLead that was meant to delete bad data but we do not seem to use ZoomInfo/Ringlead anymore).
Added a decision element that checks whether the Lead or Contact can be found before we try to delete it (Target Ids can still exist even after the related Lead/Contact has been deleted).</description>
    <environments>Default</environments>
    <interviewLabel>Lamp - Cadence Bad Data Cleanup {!$Flow.CurrentDateTime}</interviewLabel>
    <label>SCH_CadenceTracker_BadData_DeleteLeadContact</label>
    <processMetadataValues>
        <name>BuilderType</name>
        <value>
            <stringValue>LightningFlowBuilder</stringValue>
        </value>
    </processMetadataValues>
    <processMetadataValues>
        <name>CanvasMode</name>
        <value>
            <stringValue>AUTO_LAYOUT_CANVAS</stringValue>
        </value>
    </processMetadataValues>
    <processMetadataValues>
        <name>OriginBuilderType</name>
        <value>
            <stringValue>LightningFlowBuilder</stringValue>
        </value>
    </processMetadataValues>
    <processType>AutoLaunchedFlow</processType>
    <recordDeletes>
        <name>Delete_contacts</name>
        <label>Delete contacts</label>
        <locationX>578</locationX>
        <locationY>684</locationY>
        <filterLogic>and</filterLogic>
        <filters>
            <field>Id</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Record.TargetId__NotFound</elementReference>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <object>Contact</object>
    </recordDeletes>
    <recordDeletes>
        <description>Delete the Lead that was connected to the Cadence Tracker</description>
        <name>Delete_leads</name>
        <label>Delete leads</label>
        <locationX>50</locationX>
        <locationY>576</locationY>
        <filterLogic>and</filterLogic>
        <filters>
            <field>Id</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Record.TargetId__NotFound</elementReference>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <object>Lead</object>
    </recordDeletes>
    <recordLookups>
        <description>Need to attempt to get the record before deleting, because it is possible the the CadenceTargetId is populated even after the target Contact or Lead has been deleted.</description>
        <name>Get_Contact</name>
        <label>Get Contact</label>
        <locationX>710</locationX>
        <locationY>360</locationY>
        <assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>false</assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Does_Contact_Exist</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <filterLogic>and</filterLogic>
        <filters>
            <field>Id</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Record.TargetId__NotFound</elementReference>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <getFirstRecordOnly>true</getFirstRecordOnly>
        <object>Contact</object>
        <storeOutputAutomatically>true</storeOutputAutomatically>
    </recordLookups>
    <recordLookups>
        <description>Need to attempt to get the record before deleting, because it is possible the the CadenceTargetId is populated even after the target Contact or Lead has been deleted.</description>
        <name>Get_Lead</name>
        <label>Get Lead</label>
        <locationX>182</locationX>
        <locationY>360</locationY>
        <assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>false</assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Does_Lead_Exist</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <filterLogic>and</filterLogic>
        <filters>
            <field>Id</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Record.TargetId__NotFound</elementReference>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <getFirstRecordOnly>true</getFirstRecordOnly>
        <object>Lead</object>
        <storeOutputAutomatically>true</storeOutputAutomatically>
    </recordLookups>
    <recordUpdates>
        <name>Remove_contacts_from_cases</name>
        <label>Remove contacts from cases</label>
        <locationX>578</locationX>
        <locationY>576</locationY>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Delete_contacts</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <filterLogic>and</filterLogic>
        <filters>
            <field>ContactId</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Record.TargetId__NotFound</elementReference>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>ContactId</field>
        </inputAssignments>
        <object>Case</object>
    </recordUpdates>
    <start>
        <locationX>518</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Cadence_Target_Filter</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <filterLogic>and</filterLogic>
        <filters>
            <field>CompletionDisposition__NotFound</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <stringValue>Bad Data</stringValue>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <filters>
            <field>TargetId__NotFound</field>
            <operator>IsNull</operator>
            <value>
                <booleanValue>false</booleanValue>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <object>ActionCadenceTracker__NotFound</object>
        <schedule>
            <frequency>Daily</frequency>
            <startDate>2023-11-14</startDate>
            <startTime>12:50:00.000Z</startTime>
        </schedule>
        <triggerType>Scheduled</triggerType>
    </start>
    <status>Active</status>
</Flow>
